I don't know whether this could be considered a real Ascension...

I was so excited to have reached the Astral Plane for the first time in two
years of playing, that I offered the amulet to the wrong God! 
Anyway I'm really glad with the way things went!

[warning: here be spoilers!!]




Since level one I thought I was having one of those promising lucky games,
because an aligned altar was in the room right next to the upstairs.
Descending towards the oracle level lara found two more altars which she
proceeded to convert and make her "base". A deli and an armor shop provided
an AC decent enough to take on Sokoban without troubles (especially
the cloak of displacement), and lots of sacking granted Mojo and a shower of
holy water. 
Right below the Soko level, surprise surprise, was a Bigroom with the juicy
bones of a post-castle Valk (died for stuffing her face on a
troll corpse, of all things). 

After a few trips from the Bigroom to the altar-base and back, lara found
herself with an amulet of reflection, grey dragon scale armor, fooproofed
gauntlets of strenght and speed boots, rings of regeneration, levitation,
free action and slow digestion, a recharged wand of wishing, 2 magic
markers, 2 BofH, luckstone, various scrolls, potions and wands, and a
super-handy wand of cancellation to uncurse the uncursable. 
A few wishes later the lucky Valk had blessed-genocided basically half of
the dungeon population (especially h, for fear of nasty amnesias, L because
I hate them, and ; because I was drowned by a kraken once).

The rest is quick history: lara kept sacking and hacking around the dungeon
to get money for protection, points to level up for the Quest, and the
fantastic Vorpal Blade she used to get rid of Lord Surtur, which made a
nice snack too.
Soon after clearing the Castle lara got her avid hands on enchant armor,
lowered the AC to -26, and finally ditched the wooden shield and the
dwarvish helm in favour of a leather helm and two-weaponing, with the
faithful silver saber. 

The descent to the Valley and Gehennom was stressing but not hard: Asmodeus
and Baalzebub were bribed, Juiblex was surprisingly meek and didn't even
try to swallow the little Valkyrie; as for Orcus, lara couldn't be luckier
and disposed of him with a cockatrice corpse. 
The biggest waste of time was finding the stairs to Vlad's tower, while the
sanctum wasn't very hard to clear, since Rodney didn't show up at all.

Once taken the amulet, lara travelled as quick as possible to level 1, took
her Planes' kit and went for it. Rodney apperared as expected but lara
cold-bloodedly insta-killed him.

Things went very well until the Plane of Water, when lara found out the last
of her scrolls of gold detection had burnt to ashes in the Plane of Fire.
She took time to write another and use it, but in the whole concitation
stepped on the portal without removing her ring of conflict... Uh oh.
Odin must have been really angry with lara because she was surrounded by
hostile angels and, not knowing what to do, hammered them straight back to
heaven. In the following minute lara was so lost in blinding panic that she
took Famine down twice and never found out until the final credits rolled!
She wandered erratically until she got blinded and spotted two high priests:
one was really close to her, the other was far to the right and separated
from her by what looked like a thousand nasties. 
Once regained her sight, lara realized the closest priest (and altar) was
chaotic. Whatever happened to the extreme luck?
So, in fear of the hordes, and of her god's anger, lara said "Bye bye Odin"
and yelled "Hail master Loki!! I got something for you!". Loki (assuming
the appearance of Erkekjetter Silenoz in lara's imagination) accepted the
gift gracefully!

So much for the demigoddess state, but the game's over anyway. 
As credits rolled, lara thought to herself that after all, a Valkyrie who
listened exclusively to Dimmu Borgir during the whole game couldn't be but
chaotic.

